{"n":15,"title":"Worth watching?","blurb":"Comparing and recommending, and writing a review","steps":[{"stage":"Warm-up","type":"pick","title":"Which of these has happened to you?","sub":"Здесь нет правильного ответа","options":[{"label":"a friend recommended something dreadful"},{"label":"the reviews were wrong"},{"label":"the trailer was better than the film"},{"label":"everybody loved it except you"}]},{"stage":"Vocabulary","type":"cards","title":"Слова урока","sub":"Нажми на карточку, чтобы увидеть перевод","words":[{"en":"performance","pos":"n","ru":"игра, исполнение","kk":"ойын, орындау","def":"the acting or playing of one person in a film or a concert","img":"/course/b1/img/l15-performance.webp"},{"en":"disappointing","pos":"adj","ru":"разочаровывающий","kk":"көңіл қалдыратын","def":"not as good as you hoped","img":"/course/b1/img/l15-disappointing.webp"},{"en":"dreadful","pos":"adj","ru":"ужасный","kk":"сұмдық жаман","def":"extremely bad","img":"/course/b1/img/l15-dreadful.webp"},{"en":"terrifying","pos":"adj","ru":"пугающий","kk":"қорқынышты","def":"making you very frightened","img":"/course/b1/img/l15-terrifying.webp"},{"en":"unexciting","pos":"adj","ru":"скучный","kk":"қызықсыз","def":"dull; not interesting at all","img":"/course/b1/img/l15-unexciting.webp"},{"en":"amusing","pos":"adj","ru":"забавный","kk":"көңілді","def":"funny and enjoyable","img":"/course/b1/img/l15-amusing.webp"},{"en":"infuriating","pos":"adj","ru":"бесящий","kk":"ашуландыратын","def":"extremely annoying","img":"/course/b1/img/l15-infuriating.webp"},{"en":"irritation","pos":"n","ru":"раздражение","kk":"мазасыздық","def":"something small that keeps annoying you","img":"/course/b1/img/l15-irritation.webp"},{"en":"violent","pos":"adj","ru":"жестокий","kk":"зорлықты","def":"involving people hurting each other","img":"/course/b1/img/l15-violent.webp"},{"en":"astonishing","pos":"adj","ru":"поразительный","kk":"таңғаларлық","def":"extremely surprising","img":"/course/b1/img/l15-astonishing.webp"},{"en":"brilliant","pos":"adj","ru":"блестящий, отличный","kk":"керемет","def":"extremely good","img":"/course/b1/img/l15-brilliant.webp"},{"en":"incredibly","pos":"adv","ru":"невероятно","kk":"керемет","def":"extremely; used before a normal adjective","img":"/course/b1/img/l15-incredibly.webp"},{"en":"absolutely","pos":"adv","ru":"абсолютно","kk":"мүлдем","def":"completely; used before an extreme adjective","img":"/course/b1/img/l15-absolutely.webp"},{"en":"essentially","pos":"adv","ru":"по сути","kk":"негізінен","def":"in the most important way; basically","img":"/course/b1/img/l15-essentially.webp"},{"en":"magically","pos":"adv","ru":"волшебным образом","kk":"сиқырлы түрде","def":"in a way that cannot be explained, as if by magic","img":"/course/b1/img/l15-magically.webp"},{"en":"falsely","pos":"adv","ru":"ложно, ошибочно","kk":"жалған түрде","def":"wrongly; because of something untrue","img":"/course/b1/img/l15-falsely.webp"},{"en":"modern-day","pos":"adj","ru":"современный","kk":"қазіргі","def":"existing now, in our own time","img":"/course/b1/img/l15-modern-day.webp"},{"en":"middle class","pos":"n","ru":"средний класс","kk":"орта тап","def":"the group of people between the richest and the poorest","img":"/course/b1/img/l15-middle-class.webp"}]},{"stage":"Vocabulary","type":"choice","title":"Выбери правильный перевод","prompt":"performance","options":["игра, исполнение","разочаровывающий","ужасный","пугающий"],"answer":"игра, исполнение"},{"stage":"Vocabulary","type":"choice","title":"Выбери правильный перевод","prompt":"disappointing","options":["разочаровывающий","скучный","забавный","бесящий"],"answer":"разочаровывающий"},{"stage":"Vocabulary","type":"choice","title":"Выбери правильный перевод","prompt":"dreadful","options":["ужасный","раздражение","жестокий","поразительный"],"answer":"ужасный"},{"stage":"Vocabulary","type":"choice","title":"Выбери правильный перевод","prompt":"terrifying","options":["пугающий","блестящий, отличный","невероятно","абсолютно"],"answer":"пугающий"},{"stage":"Vocabulary","type":"choice","title":"Выбери правильный перевод","prompt":"unexciting","options":["скучный","по сути","волшебным образом","ложно, ошибочно"],"answer":"скучный"},{"stage":"Vocabulary","type":"choice","title":"Выбери правильный перевод","prompt":"amusing","options":["забавный","современный","средний класс","несмотря на"],"answer":"забавный"},{"stage":"Grammar","type":"note","title":"Как это работает","html":"It was <span class=\"hl\">nothing like as good as</span> I expected it to be."},{"stage":"Grammar","type":"note","title":"Как это работает","html":"It&rsquo;s <span class=\"hl\">really not worth</span> seeing."},{"stage":"Grammar","type":"note","title":"Как это работает","html":"It&rsquo;s <span class=\"hl\">much more</span> interesting <span class=\"hl\">than</span> the first one."},{"stage":"Grammar","type":"choice","title":"Which one is the strongest way of saying something was bad?","prompt":"—","options":["the first","the second","the third","the fourth"],"answer":"the fourth"},{"stage":"Practice","type":"choice","title":"Normal or extreme? Choose the adverb that goes with the adjective.","prompt":"The ending was ____ brilliant.","options":["a bit","very","absolutely"],"answer":"absolutely"},{"stage":"Practice","type":"choice","title":"Normal or extreme? Choose the adverb that goes with the adjective.","prompt":"The middle hour was ____ disappointing.","options":["quite","very much","absolutely"],"answer":"quite"},{"stage":"Practice","type":"choice","title":"Normal or extreme? Choose the adverb that goes with the adjective.","prompt":"The special effects are ____ astonishing.","options":["absolutely","very","a bit"],"answer":"absolutely"},{"stage":"Practice","type":"choice","title":"Normal or extreme? Choose the adverb that goes with the adjective.","prompt":"The cinema was ____ cold.","options":["very much","absolutely","very"],"answer":"very"},{"stage":"Speaking","type":"write","title":"Check your own review. Which of them did you do?","sub":"Напиши ответ, затем проверь себя","placeholder":"Твой ответ…","model":"Comparing: much more… than · nothing like as… as · the most… I’ve ever… · compared with…"},{"stage":"Wrap","type":"checklist","title":"Отметь, чему научился","sub":"Я могу…","items":["✓ judge a film strongly — dreadful, disappointing, astonishing, brilliant, infuriating","✓ put incredibly with normal adjectives and absolutely with extreme ones","✓ compare two things — much more… than, nothing like as… as, compared with","✓ recommend something — It’s worth…ing, I’d highly recommend…","✓ turn something down politely, three different ways","✓ write a review with a claim, a criticism, a comparison and a verdict"]}]}